Which of these use shared hashes where filtering
is necessary?


METHODS FOR EFFICIENT SOCKET ITERATION
======================================

* SOCK_HASH
* SOCK_STORAGE
  * Won't work out of the box without a few adjustments I think
    * Mark sk as PTR_TRUSTED.
    * Need to acquire socket lock before running iterator program.
    * Iterator looks like it's flaky (skips / repeats ?)
    * Also holds RCU lock between start/stop which is incompatible with lock
    * Same infinite looping bug exists here.
* Allow for socket iterators to see things in every namespace.
    * What if per-namespace hashes are used?
    * Still, we could visit each exactly once I think if we combined with
      net ns iteration?
* Generic maps or data structure using arena + bpf_sock_destroy in test prog
* Net namespace iteration in BPF?

